			"File": [
				"⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",
				797,
				300
			],
			"Message": "build(Cocoon): Revert minification to enable production debugging and align naming conventions\n\nReverse the previous aggressive minification strategy for the Cocoon extension host. Restore PascalCase naming to all ESBuild configuration constants (`BaseConfig`, `CompileConfig`, `TargetConfig`, `CocoonESBuildConfig`) to ensure maintainability and adhere to project standards. Replace opaque single-character identifiers (`i`, `d`, `f`, `o`, `e`, `t`) with explicit, descriptive names.\n\nRe-enable source map generation for the `Target/` build output directory, including full stack traces for critical services such as `RPCServer`, `MountainClient`, `FileSystemRoute`, and `TypeConverter`. Update `BaseConfig` to explicitly import environment constants (`On`, `Clean`, `Bundle`, `Compile`) from `Constant/EnvironmentConstant.js` rather than relying on implicit globals, ensuring deterministic build behavior. Update `MountainConfig.js` to use named functions (`loadMountainConfigFromEnv`, `validateMountainConfig`, `createMountainConfig`, `getMountainConfigSummary`) with enhanced TLS and connection parameter validation logic.\n\nThis change ensures that production artifacts remain debuggable for error triage while restoring a maintainable codebase structure for the build system.",
			"SHA": "0d0aaa8933bcc80a3240e50377852942eb4b0839"
		},
